-- R-Q1 (RULED 2026-09-07): under an EVERY the join line is mandatory whenever
-- there is a HENCE or a LEST. There is no default, because the barrier and the
-- fork readings differ, and a barrier default would silently reverse what a
-- single party's MAY … HENCE means today. The message names both spellings,
-- ONCE ALL HAVE and UPON EACH.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Tenant HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign HAS signer IS AN Actor

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`bare hence` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t MUST Sign (EXACTLY t) WITHIN 14 HENCE FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`bare lest` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14
        LEST   BREACH BY t
